{"id":"sfusd-other-pay-against-districts","tier":"REDFLAG","title":"The school district’s “other pay” against other large districts","question":"Why is so much of San Francisco Unified’s pay recorded as “other pay”, and is that usual for a large district?","finding":"In 2021 San Francisco Unified recorded other pay equal to 26.8% of regular pay (12,324 dollars of other pay per paid position), rank 1 of 11 districts with 5,000 or more paid positions; the middle of the others was 7.3%. It is spread across ordinary jobs: Regular Classroom Teacher $22.0 million other and lump-sum pay on $90.3 million regular pay (1,428 positions); ELD Classroom Teacher $13.0 million other and lump-sum pay on $56.8 million regular pay (886 positions); Sped IA Sh -All Impair $7.6 million other and lump-sum pay on $15.8 million regular pay (782 positions).","how":"State Controller raw export, employer type K-12 Education, the years in which the district appears (2019, 2021). The ranking and other pay per paid position use OtherPay alone. The separate per-position table column and job-title examples combine OtherPay and LumpSumPay. K–12 reporting is voluntary.","limits":"Districts book stipends, extra duty, substitute days, summer school and locally funded salary supplements differently: some put them in regular pay, some in other pay. The export does not say what the other pay was. The question is what it consists of, not whether it was paid properly.","columns":[{"k":"employer","t":"District","type":"org"},{"k":"year","t":"Year","type":"year"},{"k":"positions","t":"Paid positions","type":"int"},{"k":"otherShare","t":"Other pay as share of regular pay","type":"pct"},{"k":"lumpShare","t":"Lump sums as share of regular pay","type":"pct"},{"k":"otherPer","t":"Other pay and lump sums per paid position","type":"usd"},{"k":"otShare","t":"Overtime as share of regular pay","type":"pct"}],"rows":[{"employer":"San Francisco Unified","year":2021,"positions":10664,"regular":489670487,"overtime":164630